Parameter behavior
Parameter 4 is a network block list: the script reads the current en0 IPv4 address with ipconfig and compares it to each supplied prefix. Parameter 5 supplies the custom event used to install PSEUDO only when /usr/local/bin/pseudo is missing. If PSEUDO is already installed, the Parameter 5 policy is not called.

 
Recommended Jamf policy settings
• Execution frequency: choose the policy frequency that matches the Self Service or remediation use case.
• Trigger: make the workflow available through the intended Jamf trigger, commonly Self Service for user-driven migration.
• Scope: limit deployment to Macs that require enrollment migration and meet organizational readiness criteria.
• Script priority: place prerequisite installations before this script if swiftDialog or the Jamf binary is not already guaranteed.
• Parameter 5 dependency: confirm the configured custom event installs an executable PSEUDO binary at /usr/local/bin/pseudo and returns a meaningful exit code.
4. Workflow sequence
1. Identify the active console user and verify swiftDialog.
2. Display preparation instructions and allow the user to continue or defer.
3. Verify PSEUDO. If missing, require Parameter 5, run jamf policy -event using its configured value, and then wait for the executable to appear.
4. Validate the current network against Parameter 4.
5. Require GlobalProtect/Palo Alto VPN to be disconnected and verify direct access to the Apple enrollment endpoint.
6. Record whether the user was already an administrator.
7. Create a user-owned swiftDialog command file and display preparation progress.
8. Temporarily add the user to the local admin group when needed and verify membership using three independent checks.
9. Launch profiles renew -type enrollment in the active user context.
10. Wait for the user to finish all macOS enrollment prompts. The workflow can reopen enrollment once if requested.
11. Run jamf recon -endUsername with the active username and validate profiles status -type enrollment.
12. Remove temporary administrator membership and verify removal.
13. Wait up to 60 attempts, 10 seconds apart, for non-empty ExtensionIdentifier, AuthenticationMethod, and AccountDisplayName values in /Library/Managed Preferences/com.apple.extensiblesso.plist.
14. Launch /usr/local/bin/pseudo as root and require a zero exit code.
15. Display success only when enrollment validation and administrator cleanup are successful.
5. Security and rollback behavior
• Pre-existing administrators are never demoted by the workflow.
• Temporary administrator rights are removed on normal completion, cancellation, failure, interruption, or shell exit through the cleanup trap.
• Administrator membership is validated with dsmemberutil, dseditgroup, and the resolved group list.
• PSEUDO is not launched when ExtensionIdentifier, AuthenticationMethod, or AccountDisplayName is empty.
• The migration fails closed when required prerequisites or validation checks do not pass.
